s6: 6 <composition>
	why=A PWA reader must keep working offline, and a stale service-worker cache would keep serving the reader without the new read-aloud file at all.
	build=`tts.js` is added to the precached app shell, and the cache version is bumped so every client actually refetches it.
	evidence=A cold, offline load of the reader still finds `/js/tts.js` served from cache.
	code=|
		- [`sw.js`](../../../../public/sw.js){change=worktree show=lines lines=4:34}
	n6_1: 6.1 Precache tts.js in the service worker <leaf>
		why=`reader.js` (5.4) imports `./tts.js`; an offline load with no cached copy would fail that import.
		description=Adds `/js/tts.js` to the `APP_SHELL` array precached on install.
		build=One line inside `APP_SHELL`.
		evidence=`caches.open(CACHE_VERSION).then(cache => cache.addAll(APP_SHELL))` (install handler) then includes this path.
		code=|
			- [`APP_SHELL` entry](../../../../public/sw.js){change=worktree show=lines lines=34:34}
	n6_2: 6.2 Bump the cache version <leaf>
		why=A precache list only changes what a fresh install caches; an already-installed client keeps its old cache under the old version string until the version changes.
		description=Changes `CACHE_VERSION` from `br-v20260920001` to `br-v20260925002`.
		build=One constant.
		evidence=The service worker's activate handler deletes every cache whose key is not the current `CACHE_VERSION` or `BOOKS_CACHE`, so this bump is what makes 6.1 reach existing installs.
		code=|
			- [`CACHE_VERSION`](../../../../public/sw.js){change=worktree show=lines lines=4:4}
